[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded generated control-analysis dispatch

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This is a finite analysis-dispatch profile over the existing generated ANTLR lexer/parser and public typed simulator client, not a general ngspice interpreter. A full ngspice or third-party command interpreter remains a different integration/reuse decision and is not introduced as a production runtime dependency. The new semantic entry addresses the existing opaque COMMAND_LINE metadata gap without a Split/regex command scanner. Primary semantics/format evidence: ngspice user-manual command reference, https://ngspice.sourceforge.io/docs/ngspice-manual.pdf, and official control-language tutorial, https://ngspice.sourceforge.io/ngspice-control-language-tutorial.html; actual local native POC and immutable hashes are recorded in evidence/requested-control-profile.json.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-CONTROL-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Generated bounded ordinary analysis commands
STATEMENT: >>>
One root control block may request ordinary op/dc/ac/tran commands with literal signed SI scalar arguments. Repeated direct commands shall retain order, source ranges and independent identities. Unknown effects, vectors/substitution, separators, unsupported scopes and malformed commands shall refuse the whole program atomically. Existing standalone declaration semantics shall remain unchanged.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: ControlExtraction.cs, ControlSyntax.cs, SpiceLexer/SpiceParser grammar semantic entry and RequestedControlPreparation.cs. No original command text is forwarded to the product engine; public typed requests execute. Source numeric range capture uses the original COMMAND_LINE offsets. Whitespace/full-line comments and bounded dollar-space comments are recognized by generated tokens.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-CONTROL-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Finite retained-deck run dispatch
STATEMENT: >>>
Each admitted run invocation shall dispatch its retained unique-kind outside analysis declarations once, in the qualified native priority AC/DC/OP/TRAN. Outside declarations shall not execute implicitly merely because a control block exists. Repeated run invocations shall retain distinct identities. Duplicate outside analysis kinds and mixed direct-analysis/run registration profiles shall be explicitly refused until qualified.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Native POC verifies priority independent of source order, no implicit outside.TRAN under direct OP, and duplicate AC jobs executing in reverse source order. The first profile refuses duplicates rather than silently coalescing, last-wins filtering or inventing extra/source-ordered jobs. Mixing direct analyses with run is refused because direct analysis commands can override registered jobs used later by run. This is individual-analysis qualification, not complete control-program parity.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-CONTROL-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Explicit reporting-only omissions and state-effect refusals
STATEMENT: >>>
Only exact reporting settings noaskquit, filetype=ascii and integer numdgt1..17 may be admitted as recorded unexecuted reporting metadata. Print/plot/meas/measure/save/gnuplot/echo/rusage output commands shall be recorded as unexecuted observations. Quit may occur only after all modeled commands. Alter/reset/load/shell/write/let/define/loops/noise, physics-changing settings and other unmodeled effects shall refuse atomically rather than be ignored.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
No original file/shell or reporting command executes. Measurement vectors cannot influence typed analyses because control analysis arguments are literal-only and all state-changing commands refuse. Run is modeled explicitly, never dropped. Limits:256commands per block,256tokens/4096characters per command,128effective analyses.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-CONTROL-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Independent original-control native projection
STATEMENT: >>>
Each native job shall preserve one original analysis command in its original control envelope, or one original run command plus its retained original outside analysis card. Other analysis/control/reporting instructions shall be masked only by generated source ranges, with omissions and projection hashes retained. Only qualification-owned relative write-native.raw-all and quit instrumentation may be inserted. Complete mapped grids, units, identities and finite values remain mandatory; accuracy gaps shall remain unqualified at unchanged tolerances.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Native control RAW uses blank separators between points; the bounded RAW adapter accepts those separators without relaxing point index, column count, finite value or extra-plot checks. Owned direct/repeated-run fixtures agree independently. Original unmodified simple-meas-tran.sp executes its actual.TRAN once, but its sine reference interpolation discrepancy remains an explicit numerical disagreement. No full new928-input census is claimed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-CORPUS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-CONTROL-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Native literal token boundaries and exact reporting settings
STATEMENT: >>>
Control-semantic lexing shall refuse dollar substitution anywhere in an analysis identifier, including embedded source-name dollars, while preserving ordinary deck lexing. A unary sign in an analysis scalar shall touch its NUMBER token in the original physical text. Adjacent signed numeric arguments may remain supported where an independent native witness confirms their grid. Reporting flags and literal values shall retain unary signs during validation so only the exact unsigned allowlist is admitted.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: ControlSemantic-only CONTROL_VARIABLE lexer rule, controlNumber generated token-offset predicate, unsigned value checks in ControlExtraction. Verification: RequestedControlTests malformed/ordinary-dollar/adjacent-grid regressions;100-case FsCheck replay2393,20261103 varies sign/whitespace; RequestedControlAdmissionNativeTests independently confirms native embedded V$curplot substitution to vconst, separated-sign syntax failure and adjacent attached-sign DC grids. Failed native commands can still write a constants RAW plot; existence/zero exit is not an analysis pass. Primary source: ngspice frontend/variable.c cp_variablesubst and spicelib/parser/inpeval.c INPevaluate. Retained RED/green evidence: evidence/requested-control-admission-review.json.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: FRONTEND-CONTROL-001
